WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:21.349 align:start position:0%
 
thank you  this is more than just a ball it's the  official world cup ball more colorful  than previous editions  and it has a special name  no other object has had quite the same  impact on the stars at the tournament as  this fall  it was developed by german added as  product manager jochlen raff  three different elements inspired the  design  the most obvious are these bands around  the ball  they've got this typically brazilian  flowing shape  and they're also reminiscent of the wish  bracelets that are popular throughout  brazil  and of course you have the colors and  the star theme that plays a big role in  brazil  this is where the idea came about  the headquarters of sportswear giant  adidas near nuremberg  jochen raff's team worked more than two  and a half years on the new ball before  it went into production  alongside the new look the construction  is different too the ball surface is  made of six identical panels that are  sewn together  the more uniformly the seams are  distributed the better the ball flies to  the air  the long seams and the uniform  construction are what count  then it doesn't matter how the ball is  oriented it still has a predictable  flight path  the design underwent extensive testing  in the lab before it went to the world  cup  a special machine checked if the ball  was perfectly round and symmetrical a  mechanical kickbot was used to test the  ball's flight characteristics and  professional soccer players tried it out  too  the grocery fund was really selling the  field tests were the most time consuming  part  we consulted teams in the bundesliga and  the us  two years ago we tested the ball in  brazil  and those things took time  but once we checked off all those steps  we knew we had the best ball we could  come up with  we ask um from a local berlin soccer  team to test the ball for euromax  they practice several times a week on  this pitch in the centre of town  the design is funky and fresh and it's  colorful definitely fun to play with  it's kind of based on a golf ball  because you see this raised part here  it has more stability when you kick it  we use a similar ball every weekend it's  the bundesliga ball which isn't all that  different from this one  the surface is great a different feeling  than our training ball  forget about this old bundesliga ball  i'll take this one the bazooka is the  culmination of a long evolution this  2000 year old chinese football was  stuffed with feathers and hair  until the 1960s world cup balls were  made of strips of brown leather  adidas made the first official world cup  ball in 1970 since then each design has  been given a special name  that was the first time we had a white  ball with these black pentagons to make  it easier to see  today everyone knows the design  but that world cup was the first time we  saw it  as the years and tournaments went on the  design was refined  from leather to synthetics from black  and white to multi-colored  the adidas team also came up with a  special ball for the final match  at that point the enthusiasm has reached  an absolute peak that's why we see these  bands of color bursting out of the panel  and all the little details we wanted it  to express all that emotion like a dance  a samba or music  it all comes pouring out  the designers were inspired by shapes  used by brazilian star architect oscar  niemeyer and by their experiences during  a trip to brazil  the ball is the iconic piece of  equipment in a tournament like this  we want to imbue it with the history of  the host country as a kind of tribute  that way we can see that this was the  ball they used in brazil  whether you call it an icon a high-tech  product or just a soccer ball during the  2014 world cup at least all eyes will be  on the bazooka

